From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/16] misc: modem_v1: resolve the 3.10 config conditionals
 (unifdef, mechanical)

Mechanical step, no hand edit except the three two-line
"#if defined(CONFIG_LINK_DEVICE_LLI) && !defined(..._WITH_FSM)" blocks of
modem_main.c that unifdef cannot parse (both conditions true, kept).
Every file of the import was run through unifdef 2.12 with the stock
configuration (lineage_gts28ltexx_defconfig:1322-1348, 387):

  defined:   LINK_DEVICE_SPI LINK_DEVICE_MEMORY LINK_CONTROL_MSG_COMMAND
             LINK_DEVICE_WITH_SBD_ARCH LINK_DEVICE_LLI UMTS_MODEM_SS333
             EXYNOS_MIPI_LLI_GPIO_SIDEBAND OF LINK_POWER_MANAGEMENT
             SAMSUNG_PRODUCT_SHIP
  undefined: LINK_POWER_MANAGEMENT_WITH_FSM (dropped, SYNTHESIS.md D2),
             LINK_DEVICE_SHMEM LINK_DEVICE_NAPI LINK_CONTROL_MSG_IOSM
             LINK_DEVICE_HSIC LINK_DEVICE_C2C LINK_DEVICE_USB/PLD/MIPI/DPRAM
             SEC_MODEM_XMM7260_CAT6 LTE_MODEM_XMM7260 and the other modems
             (SS222 SS300 SH222AP XMM626x CMC22x CBP7x/82 MDM6600 ESC6270
             QSC6085 SPRD8803), SEC_MODEM_DEBUG(FS) DEBUG_PKTLOG ARGOS
             SEC_DEBUG_MIF_OOM BOOT_DEVICE_SPI COMPAT (all prefixed CONFIG_)

The only change in behaviour relative to stock is the FSM branch: the
non-FSM link-PM code of link_device_lli.c is what remains, and the next
commit replaces it with the locked-on PM of kernel_port_design.md
section 2.7.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
